 "lookahead": {
  "code_facts": [
   "signal at bar k reads close[k], close[k-1], atr[k] = mean TR[k-13..k] (TR[i] uses high/low[i], close[i-1]): all known at bar k's close; fill = open[k+1]",
   "initial stop = entry -/+ trail_k x atr[entry_bar-1] = atr[k] (the signal bar) - known before the fill",
   "stop at bar j is checked against the level set at bar j-1's close; the trail update with close[j]/atr[j] happens AFTER bar j's check and applies from bar j+1",
   "morning range = bars a..a+11 (complete at 10:30); first signal bar k = a+14 (closes 10:45), first fill bar 15 (10:45)",
   "trailing median = morning_ranges[sess-20:sess] - today excluded; morning_ranges is precomputed for all sessions but only past entries are read",
   "difference-adjusted signal arrays change nothing (raw and adjusted give the same 1396 trades): every ATR window the plugin reads starts at or after a session's 2nd bar, so a roll gap never enters a decision",
   "no size logic (1 contract), no target"
  ],
